\details{
DCP assigns its own classes to condominium billing lots whose units have
mixed classes: \code{RC} (mixed commercial), \code{RD} (mixed residential), \code{RM}
(residential and commercial), \code{RI} (commercial and industrial), \code{RX}
(residential, commercial, and industrial), and \code{RZ} (residential and
industrial). It also assigns \code{Q0} to vacant lots mapped as parks and
\code{QG} to vacant lots with community gardens.

A few codes in PLUTO 26v2 are not defined in either dictionary: \code{CB},
\code{CC}, \code{DB}, \code{DC}, \code{VC}, and \code{VG} (118 lots).
